#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "A free IBM course on quantum information and computation"
msgstr "Kursus IBM percuma tentang maklumat dan pengkomputeran kuantum"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: sidebar_label
#, no-wrap
msgid "Naimark's theorem"
msgstr "Teorem Naimark"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Naimark's theorem* is a fundamental fact concerning measurements.\n"
"It states that every general measurement can be implemented in a simple way that's reminiscent of Stinespring representations of channels:\n"
"1. The system to be measured is first combined with an initialized workspace system, forming a compound system.\n"
"2. A unitary operation is then performed on the compound system.\n"
"3. Finally, the workspace system is *measured* with respect to a *standard basis measurement*, yielding the outcome of the original general measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Teorem Naimark* adalah fakta asas tentang pengukuran.\n"
"Ia menyatakan bahawa setiap pengukuran umum boleh dilaksanakan dengan cara yang mudah yang mengingatkan representasi Stinespring bagi saluran:\n"
"1. Sistem yang akan diukur digabungkan dahulu dengan sistem ruang kerja yang dimulakan, membentuk sistem kompaun.\n"
"2. Operasi unitar kemudian dilakukan ke atas sistem kompaun.\n"
"3. Akhirnya, sistem ruang kerja *diukur* berkenaan dengan *pengukuran asas piawai*, menghasilkan hasil pengukuran umum asal.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Theorem statement and proof {#theorem-statement-and-proof}"
msgstr "Penyataan teorem dan bukti {#theorem-statement-and-proof}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let $\\mathsf{X}$ be a system and let $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ be a "
"collection of positive semidefinite matrices satisfying\n"
msgstr ""
"Biar $\\mathsf{X}$ menjadi sistem dan biar $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ "
"menjadi koleksi matriks positif semidefinit yang memenuhi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P_0 + \\cdots + P_{m-1} = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is to say that they describe a measurement of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Also let $\\mathsf{Y}$ be a system whose classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ which is the set of possible outcomes of this measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"ertinya ia menerangkan pengukuran $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Juga biar $\\mathsf{Y}$ menjadi sistem yang set keadaan klasikalnya ialah $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\},$ iaitu set hasil yang mungkin bagi pengukuran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Naimark's theorem states that there exists a unitary operation $U$ on the "
"compound system $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ so that the implementation "
"suggested by the following figure yields measurement outcomes that agree "
"with the given measurement $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\},$ meaning that the "
"probabilities for the different possible measurement outcomes are precisely "
"in agreement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Teorem Naimark menyatakan bahawa terdapat operasi unitar $U$ pada sistem "
"kompaun $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ supaya pelaksanaan yang dicadangkan oleh"
" rajah berikut menghasilkan hasil pengukuran yang selaras dengan pengukuran "
"yang diberikan $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\},$ bermakna kebarangkalian untuk "
"hasil pengukuran yang berbeza adalah tepat sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![An implementation of a general measurement as in Naimark's "
"theorem](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/Naimark.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Pelaksanaan pengukuran umum seperti dalam teorem "
"Naimark](/learning/images/courses/general-formulation-of-quantum-"
"information/general-measurements/Naimark.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, the system $\\mathsf{X}$ starts out in some arbitrary state $\\rho$ while $\\mathsf{Y}$ is initialized to the $\\vert 0\\rangle$ state.\n"
"The unitary operation $U$ is applied to $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ and then the system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is measured with a standard basis measurement, yielding some outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk jelas, sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ bermula dalam beberapa keadaan sewenang-wenangnya $\\rho$ manakala $\\mathsf{Y}$ dimulakan kepada keadaan $\\vert 0\\rangle$.\n"
"Operasi unitar $U$ diterapkan ke atas $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ dan kemudian sistem $\\mathsf{Y}$ diukur dengan pengukuran asas piawai, menghasilkan beberapa hasil $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The system $\\mathsf{X}$ is pictured as part of the output of the circuit, but for now we won't concern ourselves with the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ after $U$ is performed, and can imagine that it is traced out.\n"
"We'll be interested in the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ after $U$ is performed later in the lesson, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ digambarkan sebagai sebahagian dari output litar, tetapi buat masa ini kita tidak akan mempersoalkan keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ selepas $U$ dilakukan, dan boleh bayangkan bahawa ia dikesan keluar.\n"
"Kita akan berminat dengan keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ selepas $U$ dilakukan kemudian dalam pelajaran ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An implementation of a measurement in this way is clearly reminiscent of a Stinespring representation of a channel, and the mathematical underpinnings are similar as well.\n"
"The difference here is that the workspace system is measured rather than being traced out like in the case of a Stinespring representation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pelaksanaan pengukuran dengan cara ini jelas mengingatkan representasi Stinespring bagi saluran, dan asas matematiknya juga serupa.\n"
"Perbezaannya di sini ialah sistem ruang kerja diukur bukannya dikesan keluar seperti dalam kes representasi Stinespring.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The fact that every measurement can be implemented in this way is pretty "
"simple to prove, but we're going to need a fact concerning positive "
"semidefinite matrices first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Fakta bahawa setiap pengukuran boleh dilaksanakan dengan cara ini agak mudah"
" untuk dibuktikan, tetapi kita perlu mengetahui fakta tentang matriks "
"positif semidefinit terlebih dahulu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Figure title=\"Fact\">\n"
"Suppose $P$ is an $n \\times n$ positive semidefinite matrix. There exists a unique $n\\times n$ positive semidefinite matrix $Q$ for which $Q^2 = P.$ This unique positive semidefinite matrix is called the *square root* of $P$ and is denoted $\\sqrt{P}.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Figure title=\"Fakta\">\n"
"Andaikan $P$ adalah matriks positif semidefinit $n \\times n$. Terdapat matriks positif semidefinit $n\\times n$ yang unik $Q$ di mana $Q^2 = P.$ Matriks positif semidefinit unik ini dipanggil *punca kuasa dua* bagi $P$ dan ditulis $\\sqrt{P}.$\n"
"</Figure>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to find the square root of a positive semidefinite matrix is to "
"first compute a spectral decomposition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu cara untuk mencari punca kuasa dua bagi matriks positif semidefinit "
"adalah dengan mengira penguraian spektrum terlebih dahulu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"P = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"P = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because $P$ is positive semidefinite, its eigenvalues must be nonnegative "
"real numbers, and by replacing them with their square roots we obtain an "
"expression for the square root of $P.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kerana $P$ adalah positif semidefinit, nilai eigennya mestilah nombor nyata "
"tidak negatif, dan dengan menggantikannya dengan punca kuasa dua kita "
"mendapat ungkapan untuk punca kuasa dua bagi $P.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{P} = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sqrt{P} = \\sum_{k=0}^{n-1} \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"With this concept in hand, we're ready to prove Naimark's theorem.\n"
"Under the assumption that $\\mathsf{X}$ has $n$ classical states, a unitary operation $U$ on the pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ can be represented by an $nm\\times nm$ matrix, which we can view as an $m\\times m$ block matrix whose blocks are $n\\times n.$\n"
"The key to the proof is to take $U$ to be any unitary matrix that matches the following pattern.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan konsep ini, kita sudah bersedia untuk membuktikan teorem Naimark.\n"
"Dengan andaian bahawa $\\mathsf{X}$ mempunyai $n$ keadaan klasikal, operasi unitar $U$ pada pasangan $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ boleh diwakili oleh matriks $nm\\times nm,$ yang boleh kita pandang sebagai matriks blok $m\\times m$ yang blok-bloknya berukuran $n\\times n.$\n"
"Kunci bukti adalah mengambil $U$ sebagai sebarang matriks unitar yang sepadan dengan corak berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For it to be possible to fill in the blocks marked with a question mark so that $U$ is unitary, it's both necessary and sufficient that the first $n$ columns, which are formed by the blocks $\\sqrt{P_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{P_{m-1}},$ are orthonormal.\n"
"We can then use the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process to fill in the remaining columns, just like we encountered in the previous lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"Agar boleh mengisi blok yang ditanda dengan tanda tanya supaya $U$ adalah unitar, perlu dan memadai bahawa $n$ lajur pertama, yang terbentuk daripada blok $\\sqrt{P_0},\\ldots,\\sqrt{P_{m-1}},$ adalah ortonormal.\n"
"Kita kemudiannya boleh menggunakan proses ortogonalisasi Gram-Schmidt untuk mengisi lajur yang selebihnya, sama seperti yang kita jumpai dalam pelajaran sebelumnya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The first $n$ columns of $U$ can be expressed as vectors in the following "
"way, where $c = 0,\\ldots,n-1$ refers to the column number starting from "
"$0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"$n$ lajur pertama $U$ boleh dinyatakan sebagai vektor dengan cara berikut, "
"di mana $c = 0,\\ldots,n-1$ merujuk kepada nombor lajur bermula dari $0.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_c\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\vert c\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\gamma_c\\rangle = \\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\vert c\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We can compute the inner product between any two of them as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita boleh mengira hasil darab dalam antara mana-mana dua daripadanya "
"seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_c \\vert \\gamma_d \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle \\cdot \\langle c \\vert \\sqrt{P_a}\\sqrt{P_b}\\, \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a \\Biggr) \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_c \\vert \\gamma_d \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{a,b = 0}^{m-1} \\langle a \\vert b \\rangle \\cdot \\langle c \\vert \\sqrt{P_a}\\sqrt{P_b}\\, \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert \\Biggl(\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1}  P_a \\Biggr) \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"= \\langle c \\vert d\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This shows that these columns are in fact orthonormal, so we can fill in the"
" remaining columns of $U$ in a way that guarantees the entire matrix is "
"unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ini menunjukkan bahawa lajur-lajur ini sebenarnya ortonormal, jadi kita "
"boleh mengisi lajur yang selebihnya bagi $U$ dengan cara yang menjamin "
"keseluruhan matriks adalah unitar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to check that the measurement outcome probabilities for the simulation are consistent with the original measurement.\n"
"For a given initial state $\\rho$ of $\\mathsf{X},$ the measurement described by the collection $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ results in each outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinggal untuk memeriksa bahawa kebarangkalian hasil pengukuran bagi simulasi adalah konsisten dengan pengukuran asal.\n"
"Untuk keadaan awal $\\rho$ bagi $\\mathsf{X}$ yang diberikan, pengukuran yang diterangkan oleh koleksi $\\{P_0,\\ldots,P_{m-1}\\}$ menghasilkan setiap hasil $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ dengan kebarangkalian $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To obtain the outcome probabilities for the simulation, let's first give the name $\\sigma$ to the state of $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ after $U$ has been performed.\n"
"This state can be expressed as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Untuk mendapatkan kebarangkalian hasil bagi simulasi, pertama-tama mari kita namakan $\\sigma$ sebagai keadaan $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ selepas $U$ dilakukan.\n"
"Keadaan ini boleh dinyatakan seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalently, in a block matrix form, we have the following equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara ekuivalen, dalam bentuk matriks blok, kita mempunyai persamaan "
"berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sigma & =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\rho & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\sqrt{P_1} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\sigma & =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\rho & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0 \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\cdots & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0} & \\sqrt{P_1} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\fbox{?} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\\\\[5mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_0}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_0} & \\cdots & \\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\\rho\\sqrt{P_{m-1}}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Notice that the entries of $U$ falling into the blocks marked with a question mark have no influence on the outcome by virtue of the fact that we're conjugating a matrix of the form $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$\n"
"— so the question mark entries are always multiplied by zero entries of $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$ when the matrix product is computed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa entri $U$ yang jatuh ke dalam blok yang ditanda dengan tanda tanya tidak memberi sebarang pengaruh terhadap hasil kerana kita sedang menkonjugat matriks berbentuk $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$\n"
"— jadi entri tanda tanya selalu didarab dengan entri sifar bagi $\\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho$ apabila hasil darab matriks dikira.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we can analyze what happens when a standard basis measurement is performed on $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"The probabilities of the possible outcomes are given by the diagonal entries of the reduced state $\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}}$ of $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kini kita boleh menganalisis apa yang berlaku apabila pengukuran asas piawai dilakukan ke atas $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"
"Kebarangkalian hasil yang mungkin diberikan oleh entri pepenjuru keadaan tereduksi $\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}}$ bagi $\\mathsf{Y}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} = \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\\Bigr) \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} = \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\\Bigr) \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, using the cyclic property of the trace, we see that the "
"probability to obtain a given outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ is as "
"follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Khususnya, dengan menggunakan sifat kitaran surih, kita dapat melihat bahawa"
" kebarangkalian untuk mendapatkan hasil tertentu $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ "
"adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}\\Bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\sigma_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\Bigl(\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}\\Bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This matches with the original measurement, establishing the correctness of "
"the simulation.\n"
msgstr "Ini sesuai dengan pengukuran asal, menetapkan ketepatan simulasi.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Non-destructive measurements {#non-destructive-measurements}"
msgstr "Pengukuran tidak musnah {#non-destructive-measurements}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So far in the lesson, we've concerned ourselves with *destructive* "
"measurements, where the output consists of the classical measurement result "
"alone and there is no specification of the post-measurement quantum state of"
" the system that was measured.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sejauh ini dalam pelajaran ini, kita telah memperhatikan *pengukuran "
"musnah*, di mana output hanya terdiri daripada hasil pengukuran klasikal dan"
" tiada spesifikasi keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran sistem yang diukur.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Non-destructive* measurements, on the other hand, do precisely this.\n"
"Specifically, non-destructive measurements describe not only the classical measurement outcome probabilities, but also the state of the system that was measured conditioned on each possible measurement outcome.\n"
"Note that the term *non-destructive* refers to the *system* being measured but not necessarily its state, which could change significantly as a result of the measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Pengukuran tidak musnah*, sebaliknya, melakukan perkara ini dengan tepat.\n"
"Khususnya, pengukuran tidak musnah menerangkan bukan sahaja kebarangkalian hasil pengukuran klasikal, tetapi juga keadaan sistem yang diukur bagi setiap hasil pengukuran yang mungkin.\n"
"Perhatikan bahawa istilah *tidak musnah* merujuk kepada *sistem* yang diukur tetapi tidak semestinya keadaannya, yang boleh berubah dengan ketara akibat pengukuran.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, for a given destructive measurement, there will be multiple (in fact infinitely many) non-destructive measurements that are *compatible* with the given destructive measurement, meaning that the classical measurement outcome probabilities match precisely with the destructive measurement.\n"
"So, there isn't a unique way to define the post-measurement quantum state of a system for a given measurement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Secara umum, untuk pengukuran musnah yang diberikan, akan ada pelbagai (malah tak terhingga banyak) pengukuran tidak musnah yang *serasi* dengan pengukuran musnah yang diberikan, bermakna kebarangkalian hasil pengukuran klasikal sepadan dengan tepat dengan pengukuran musnah.\n"
"Jadi, tidak ada cara yang unik untuk mentakrifkan keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran suatu sistem bagi pengukuran yang diberikan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, in fact, possible to generalize non-destructive measurements even "
"further, so that they produce a classical measurement outcome along with a "
"quantum state output of a system that isn't necessarily the same as the "
"input system.\n"
msgstr ""
"Malah, adalah mungkin untuk mengitlakkan pengukuran tidak musnah lebih jauh,"
" supaya ia menghasilkan hasil pengukuran klasikal bersama output keadaan "
"kuantum suatu sistem yang tidak semestinya sama dengan sistem input.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The notion of a non-destructive measurement is an interesting and useful abstraction.\n"
"It should, however, be recognized that non-destructive measurements can always be described as compositions of channels and destructive measurements — so there is a sense in which the notion of a destructive measurement is the more fundamental one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Konsep pengukuran tidak musnah adalah abstraksi yang menarik dan berguna.\n"
"Namun, perlu diakui bahawa pengukuran tidak musnah boleh sentiasa diterangkan sebagai komposisi saluran dan pengukuran musnah — jadi ada suatu pengertian di mana konsep pengukuran musnah adalah yang lebih asas.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From Naimark's theorem {#from-naimarks-theorem}"
msgstr "Daripada teorem Naimark {#from-naimarks-theorem}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the simulation of a general measurement like we have in Naimark's theorem.\n"
"A simple way to obtain a non-destructive measurement from this simulation is revealed by the figure from before, where the system $\\mathsf{X}$ is not traced out, but is part of the output.\n"
"This yields both a classical measurement outcome $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ as well as a post-measurement quantum state of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Pertimbangkan simulasi pengukuran umum seperti yang ada dalam teorem Naimark.\n"
"Cara mudah untuk mendapatkan pengukuran tidak musnah daripada simulasi ini didedahkan oleh rajah sebelumnya, di mana sistem $\\mathsf{X}$ tidak dikesan keluar, tetapi merupakan sebahagian daripada output.\n"
"Ini menghasilkan hasil pengukuran klasikal $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ serta keadaan kuantum pasca-pengukuran bagi $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's describe these states in mathematical terms.\n"
"We're assuming that the initial state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\rho,$ so that after the initialized system $\\mathsf{Y}$ is introduced and $U$ is performed, we have that $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ is in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita terangkan keadaan ini dalam istilah matematik.\n"
"Kita andaikan bahawa keadaan awal $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah $\\rho,$ sehingga selepas sistem $\\mathsf{Y}$ yang dimulakan diperkenalkan dan $U$ dilakukan, kita mempunyai bahawa $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ berada dalam keadaan\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sigma =\n"
"U \\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho\\bigr) U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The probabilities for the different classical outcomes to appear are the same as before — they can't change as a result of us deciding to ignore or not ignore $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"That is, we obtain each $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ with probability $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Kebarangkalian untuk hasil klasikal yang berbeza adalah sama seperti sebelumnya — ia tidak boleh berubah akibat keputusan kita untuk mengabaikan atau tidak mengabaikan $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Iaitu, kita mendapatkan setiap $a\\in\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}$ dengan kebarangkalian $\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho).$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Conditioned upon having obtained a particular measurement outcome $a,$ the "
"resulting state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is given by this expression.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bersyarat pada mendapat hasil pengukuran tertentu $a,$ keadaan yang terhasil"
" bagi $\\mathsf{X}$ diberikan oleh ungkapan ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to see this is to represent a standard basis measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ by the completely dephasing channel $\\Delta_m,$ where the channel output describes classical measurement outcomes as (diagonal) density matrices.\n"
"An expression of the state we obtain is as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Satu cara untuk melihat ini adalah dengan mewakili pengukuran asas piawai bagi $\\mathsf{Y}$ oleh saluran penyahfas sepenuhnya $\\Delta_m,$ di mana output saluran menerangkan hasil pengukuran klasikal sebagai matriks ketumpatan (pepenjuru).\n"
"Ungkapan keadaan yang kita peroleh adalah seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\Delta_m(\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert) \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"= \\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a,b=0}^{m-1} \\Delta_m(\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert) \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_b}\n"
"= \\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can then write this state as a convex combination of product states,\n"
msgstr ""
"Kita kemudiannya boleh menulis keadaan ini sebagai gabungan cembung bagi "
"keadaan hasil,\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\\, \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)\\, \\vert a\\rangle \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\frac{\\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)},\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which is consistent with the expression we've obtained for the state of "
"$\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on each possible measurement outcome.\n"
msgstr ""
"yang konsisten dengan ungkapan yang kita peroleh untuk keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$"
" bersyarat pada setiap hasil pengukuran yang mungkin.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "From a Kraus representation {#from-a-kraus-representation}"
msgstr "Daripada representasi Kraus {#from-a-kraus-representation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are alternative selections for $U$ in the context of Naimark's theorem"
" that produce the same measurement outcome probabilities but give entirely "
"different output states of $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat pilihan alternatif untuk $U$ dalam konteks teorem Naimark yang "
"menghasilkan kebarangkalian hasil pengukuran yang sama tetapi memberikan "
"keadaan output yang sama sekali berbeza bagi $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For instance, one option is to substitute $(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes V) U$ for $U,$ where $V$ is any unitary operation on $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"The application of $V$ to $\\mathsf{X}$ commutes with the measurement of $\\mathsf{Y}$ so the classical outcome probabilities do not change, but now the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on the outcome $a$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagai contoh, satu pilihan adalah menggantikan $(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}} \\otimes V) U$ untuk $U,$ di mana $V$ adalah sebarang operasi unitar ke atas $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Penerapan $V$ ke atas $\\mathsf{X}$ bertukar-tukar dengan pengukuran $\\mathsf{Y}$ jadi kebarangkalian hasil klasikal tidak berubah, tetapi kini keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ bersyarat pada hasil $a$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, we could replace $U$ by the unitary matrix\n"
msgstr "Secara lebih umum, kita boleh menggantikan $U$ oleh matriks unitar\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert \\otimes V_a\\Biggr) U\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{a=0}^{m-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert \\otimes V_a\\Biggr) U\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for any choice of unitary operations $V_0,\\ldots,V_{m-1}$ on $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Again, the classical outcome probabilities are unchanged, but now the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ conditioned on the outcome $a$ becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"untuk sebarang pilihan operasi unitar $V_0,\\ldots,V_{m-1}$ ke atas $\\mathsf{X}.$\n"
"Sekali lagi, kebarangkalian hasil klasikal tidak berubah, tetapi kini keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ bersyarat pada hasil $a$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V_a \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{V_a \\sqrt{P_a} \\rho \\sqrt{P_a}V_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(P_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An equivalent way to express this freedom is connected with Kraus representations.\n"
"That is, we can describe an $m$-outcome non-destructive measurement of a system having $n$ classical states by a selection of $n\\times n$ Kraus matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ satisfying the typical condition for Kraus matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Cara setara untuk menyatakan kebebasan ini dikaitkan dengan representasi Kraus.\n"
"Iaitu, kita boleh menerangkan pengukuran tidak musnah $m$-hasil bagi sistem yang mempunyai $n$ keadaan klasikal dengan pemilihan matriks Kraus $n\\times n$ $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ yang memenuhi syarat biasa bagi matriks Kraus.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} A_a^{\\dagger} A_a = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{a = 0}^{m-1} A_a^{\\dagger} A_a = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assuming that the initial state of $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\rho,$ the classical "
"measurement outcome is $a$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Dengan andaian bahawa keadaan awal $\\mathsf{X}$ adalah $\\rho,$ hasil "
"pengukuran klasikal adalah $a$ dengan kebarangkalian\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a^{\\dagger} A_a \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"= \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(A_a^{\\dagger} A_a \\rho \\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and conditioned upon the outcome being $a$ the state of $\\mathsf{X}$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr "dan bersyarat pada hasil $a$ keadaan $\\mathsf{X}$ menjadi\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(A_a^{\\dagger}A_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{A_a \\rho A_a^{\\dagger}}{\\operatorname{Tr}(A_a^{\\dagger}A_a \\rho)}.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that this is equivalent to choosing the unitary operation $U$ in "
"Naimark's theorem as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Perhatikan bahawa ini setara dengan memilih operasi unitar $U$ dalam teorem "
"Naimark seperti berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{m-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the previous lesson we observed that the columns formed by the blocks $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ are necessarily orthogonal, by virtue of the\n"
"condition $(1).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Dalam pelajaran sebelumnya kita perhatikan bahawa lajur yang terbentuk daripada blok $A_0,\\ldots,A_{m-1}$ semestinya ortogon, berdasarkan\n"
"syarat $(1).$\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generalizations {#generalizations}"
msgstr "Pengitlakan {#generalizations}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are even more general ways to formulate non-destructive measurements than the ways we've discussed.\n"
"The notion of a *quantum instrument* (which won't be described here) represents one way to do this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Terdapat cara yang lebih umum lagi untuk merumuskan pengukuran tidak musnah berbanding cara yang telah kita bincangkan.\n"
"Konsep *instrumen kuantum* (yang tidak akan diterangkan di sini) merupakan satu cara untuk melakukan ini.\n"
